Create a highly polished vertical 9:16 Chinese narrative illustration poster with an expansive warm parchment-colored background and a strongly centered, vertically stacked composition.

The main subject is a tall, very slim ancient Chinese wandering swordsman or traveling martial artist standing upright in the center of the frame. His body proportions are intentionally elongated and elegant rather than realistic: long forearms, narrow torso, long robe silhouette, angular neck and sharply simplified limbs. His head turns toward viewer-left in profile-three-quarter view. He has a long angular face, pointed chin, prominent nose, thin arched brows, a cheerful slightly mischievous smile and clean graphic facial planes. His black hair is gathered into a high stylized topknot with pointed fan-like shapes, secured by a thin turquoise-blue headband.

His raised right arm bends sharply upward so that he is drinking from a short cylindrical beige-gold travel flask held directly to his lips. His left forearm crosses his abdomen and supports a very large semicircular slice of watermelon, bright coral-red flesh with a few sparse black seeds, a pale rind band and dark green outer skin. The watermelon should act as the strongest warm-color focal accent in the upper-middle body area.

Dress him in layered traditional Chinese robes built from large geometric color planes. Use pale icy blue for the inner sleeves, saturated cyan and turquoise for the main robe, deep teal and blue-black for the lapels and inner panels, plus narrow green and jade accents near the lower hem. The sleeves are oversized and angular, folding into broad polygonal shapes rather than realistic fabric wrinkles. Add understated dark swirling decorative motifs to selected lapel and vertical robe panels, keeping ornament elegant and sparse.

Build a humorous traveling-warrior silhouette with multiple objects arranged around his back and waist. Behind the shoulders, show several thin rod-like weapon or tool handles rising diagonally upward. Across the waist and rear silhouette place a long horizontal sword or scabbard extending toward viewer-right, a large curved blade extending toward viewer-left, another decorated sword hilt, small hanging gourd-like containers, cords, tassels and compact travel accessories. Keep all objects clearly separated and structurally readable rather than cluttered.

Behind and below the swordsman, place two stylized sighthound-like dogs. The rear dog is tan, tall and extremely thin, standing behind the man's legs toward viewer-left. Give it very long straight legs, narrow torso, extremely long pointed muzzle, triangular upright ears, small graphic eye and simple brown geometric markings. The foreground dog is very dark brown to nearly black, positioned lower-right and bending dramatically downward with its front legs extended and head close to the ground. Its spine forms a large exaggerated arch, and its long tail curves upward and backward in a clean crescent. It is eating or sniffing a discarded watermelon rind.

Scatter two or three curved watermelon rind pieces near the dogs, using coral red and jade green as small repeating visual accents.

Behind the lower half of the figure, create a field of thin stylized autumn reeds or pampas-like grasses, using ochre, pale gold, cream and muted green linear shapes. Keep them graphic and transparent enough that they do not compete with the main figure. Across the middle background, add a few extremely simple horizontal white cloud forms made from narrow flat bands. The environment should remain mostly empty, with no architecture and no realistic landscape depth.

Use a very large area of untouched warm beige negative space, especially throughout the upper third and outer edges of the poster. Add only a few tiny floating orange-red leaf or petal marks for rhythm. The background should carry subtle handmade paper fibers, mild yellowing, faint mottling and delicate vintage print grain.

Place one narrow vertical red seal-style label beside the figure around lower torso height and one smaller square red seal beneath it. At the bottom margin, arrange small restrained editorial credit typography in a single horizontal line. Typography and seals should behave as secondary graphic elements and never overpower the illustration.

Composition:
the swordsman's head sits slightly above the vertical centerline;
his raised drinking hand creates the upper-left visual extension;
the watermelon anchors the center;
the long robe creates the central vertical column;
the dogs and reeds create a broad grounded triangular base;
weapons extend laterally to counterbalance the otherwise narrow vertical composition;
large negative space occupies approximately the upper 35–40% of the frame.

Rendering language:
contemporary Chinese graphic illustration, editorial poster design, geometric flat-color construction, sophisticated elongated caricature, clean vector-like silhouettes, sharp polygonal folds, selective soft gradient transitions, restrained decorative linework, vintage Chinese print-poster atmosphere, subtle mid-century illustration influence, mild Art-Deco structural elegance, handmade paper surface.

Do not use loose watercolor washes as the main rendering method. Do not use traditional ink-brush painting as the dominant style. Do not turn the character into realistic historical costume photography. The visual identity comes from precise flat shapes, controlled color blocking, angular anatomy, graphic exaggeration and sophisticated negative-space design.

Color system:
background — warm cream, parchment beige, pale ochre;
main clothing — icy cyan, sky blue, turquoise, jade, teal, deep blue-green;
skin — stylized pale warm pink with coral shadow planes;
watermelon — saturated coral-red with green rind;
dogs — warm tan and very dark brown-black;
small accents — muted orange-red and seal red.

Lighting architecture:
a broad diffuse warm key from upper-left/front covers the composition evenly;
shading is represented by graphic color planes rather than physically realistic illumination;
shadow edges are clean and designed, not photographic;
contact shadows are limited to the feet, animals and ground line;
fill is high, approximately 1.5:1 to 2:1;
no visible rim light or dramatic backlight;
lit parchment areas remain warm while blue-green clothing shadow planes stay slightly cooler;
overall exposure is high-key with gently lifted shadows and no crushed black regions.

Preserve the source's balance between elegance and humor: the ancient traveler should feel relaxed, playful and worldly rather than heroic, solemn or aggressive.

Strict style lock:
T1 flat 2D only; smooth matte printed surfaces; no photorealism, no cinematic live-action rendering, no realistic skin pores, no visible cloth fibers, no glossy plastic 3D, no Pixar-like volume, no game CG, no heavy volumetric light, no dramatic atmospheric fog, no hyper-detailed armor, no excessive ornamental clutter, no realistic muscular anatomy, no generic anime face, no thick black comic outlines.
